<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Scaling behavior of Gemini-2.5-flash</h2>

<figure id="A8.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01279v1/scaling_flash_only.svg" id="A8.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/170;" width="381" height="170"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A8.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Scaling behavior of HLE scores in Gemini-2.5-flash relative to inference cost and total token count across different tool-augmented test-time scaling methods, where the token count includes both input and output tokens.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>LLM token confidence of generated responses</h2>

<figure id="A9.F13" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01279v1/logprob_compare.svg" id="A9.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/251;" width="333" height="251"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A9.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A9.F13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Distribution of LLM response confidence for correct and wrong answers. The response confidence is calculated based on the average token probability of the whole generated response. Here we use the responses of agent <span id="A9.F13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CoT</span> as representative, as we find the distribution characteristics are very close among different agents.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
